{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CsdzKEkYmvizJbxvCJBJ8u","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-0600-tune-vpmm-page-size-for-whir\n2\t\n3\tTune the VPMM page size to recover the 28ms WHIR regression (100ms → 128ms at APC 300) that appeared after increasing page size from 2 MiB to 16 MiB. The 16 MiB change gave a net -186ms improvement by reducing cuMemCreate overhead and routing medium allocations through cudaMallocAsync, but WHIR regressed because its 2-4 MiB buffers moved from VPMM to cudaMallocAsync. Test intermediate page sizes (4, 8, 10, 12 MiB) to find a sweet spot that preserves the large-allocation benefits while keeping WHIR buffers in VPMM. The existing VPMM_PAGE_SIZE environment variable enables rapid testing without code changes.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"837f9620-295c-4b13-9dd6-cb7faa8e25bd","uuid":"94ff2921-e185-4ce5-8092-c1d1c7be158a","timestamp":"2026-04-16T04:37:55.087Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-16-0600-tune-vpmm-page-size-for-whir\n\nTune the VPMM page size to recover the 28ms WHIR regression (100ms → 128ms at APC 300) that appeared after increasing page size from 2 MiB to 16 MiB. The 16 MiB change gave a net -186ms improvement by reducing cuMemCreate overhead and routing medium allocations through cudaMallocAsync, but WHIR regressed because its 2-4 MiB buffers moved from VPMM to cudaMallocAsync. Test intermediate page sizes (4, 8, 10, 12 MiB) to find a sweet spot that preserves the large-allocation benefits while keeping WHIR buffers in VPMM. The existing VPMM_PAGE_SIZE environment variable enables rapid testing without code changes.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
