{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CjVoXZG77sG2vH2eGiQ2zW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"8 MiB at APC 0:\n- STARK excl trace: 1898ms (vs current 16 MiB: 1804ms = +94ms regression!)\n- LogUp GKR: 818ms (vs current 718ms = +100ms)\n- WHIR: 218ms (vs current 219ms = -1ms, noise)\n- Trace Commit: 477ms (vs 476ms, noise)\n\nSo at APC 0, the 8 MiB page size causes a massive +94ms regression in STARK excl trace, almost entirely from LogUp GKR (+100ms). \n\nThis would blow past the 20ms rollback threshold. The pattern's clear: smaller pages wreck GKR performance through VPMM pool state disruption, especially at APC 0 where GKR is the bottleneck. No intermediate page size actually wins overall—the 25ms WHIR regression at APC 300 is worth accepting to keep 16 MiB as the baseline. Even though the data says to stick with what we have, I'll still implement the 4× multiplier change as planned since that was the closest candidate to test.\n\nBut wait, I need to reread the task requirements more carefully. The instructions say to keep iterating until either the success criteria are met or I'm convinced the approach won't work. I'm convinced now. The plan explicitly states: if no page size improves STARK excl trace at APC 300 by at least 10ms, keep 16 MiB unchanged. And the critical requirements say I must implement the optimization, then if it doesn't improve performance, commit it and revert it. So I'll implement the 8 MiB change, measure it, commit it, then revert since it doesn't actually help.\n\nThe implementation itself is straightforward—just changing the multiplier from 16 to 4 in the granularity calculation. Let me make that change, rebuild, run the formal after measurements, and then proceed with the commit and revert.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":920,"cache_read_input_tokens":68849,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":920},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"837f9620-295c-4b13-9dd6-cb7faa8e25bd","uuid":"f7cd2568-6f9e-46f1-a5b8-303941afda55"}
